 @flightsimdev  Well, I made a profile in MSI afterburner for high efficiency. First I did an automatic scan, then I picked a low voltage point where the frequency is high. This turned out to be 0.885 V at 2565 GHz on my card. Then I simply capped the voltage to 0.885 V.

Obviously the card doesn't get up to full speed like this. But an old game like Fallout 4 on ultra settings runs smoothly, using only 29 W. The maximum temperature is 41C with the fans at 1700 RPM (50%).

For more performance it just takes a few mouse clicks in MSI Afterburner. :)

