 @uponeric36  I'm not sure that's a totally fair comparison... Sure the 2070 is four years old, but we also had two years of massive labor/material shortages followed by a year of massive inflation. If you don't think that's going to impact generational R&D and performance uplifts / value... I'm not sure what to tell ya. Don't get me wrong, I have no love for nVidia... but this generation of GPUs was fucked from day one. 

As far as pricing, it's certainly not a great value proposition for anybody who already owns a comparable 2xxx or 3xxx GPU, but it's not terrible for a new build. Adjusted for inflation, it's that same street price as a similar midrange card like the 8GB RX580 or the 6GB 1060 from 5-6 years ago and it's a MUCH better value then what the 3060ti was selling for at release (and that's MSRP, not scalpers. A cheap 3060ti was $400 MSRP / $470 adjust for inflation). 

A pretty large chunk of what people are calling "greed" is simple inflation. I'm not yelling at my local farmer because a dozen eggs have doubled in price over the last two years... it just is what it is. Thankfully things are starting to correct, GDDR6 prices are tumbling, new fab capacity is going to be coming online to offset the always sticky Taiwan situation... I'll give AMD / NV / Intel a pandemic mulligan for this generation.

